  "1_pins": "PASS: every data pin registered in RTL (r3 pin stages unchanged: pinrow / pinbeat / straps / u_lands / u_xgi / u_xpi / gin u_gi1 in; row_e / beat / u_xbo / u_xgo / u_xpo / u_gs out); each pin belongs to ONE region (clock_entry_domains), region clock pins on the W face beside each region; r4sp pin ranges kept.",
  "2_reach": "rl1 / bk1 / straps / gather / xb crossing hops as r3 within a region; every region seam is a landing (E=2 multicycle ring -> read, <= ~750 um over 2 cycles); actual route timing decides (no FIRM stations in r5 v1: r3 station patterns name the old hierarchy).",
  "3_fanout": "r3 kept copies (xq NIPV 24 / k_oh 16, go k_b/k_p, pub rpp 16) unchanged; landings chunked 24 b (kept per-chunk counters / selectors), reset forest leaves <= 32 loads; pre-gate native census decides.",
  "4_depth": "PASS: cut only at existing register stages (xq stage-2 bundles, column / merge outputs); landing read is a registered slot mux; no new combinational path.",
  "5_storage": "PASS: unchanged hard SRAM children (x store, PV merge, columns); landing rings D=4 slots of flops.",
  "6_floorplan": "r4sp outline 691.2 x 1252.8 and child placement unchanged (8 children on the 43.2 lattice); +15556 landing flops (~4.7k um2) in the existing W / E / centre channels.",
  "7_clock": "2 regional CTS roots (ck_c, ck_x): x store region (child refs 453-529 TT) apart from the columns (104-188) (PV merge 263-313 shares the column root); every region crossing landed (lp audit PASS, 8 landings), 1-bit reset runs only; judged per region.",
  "8_schedule": "static; reschedule +3 edges per landed net, absorbed in r3 pads where possible; vs r3 halves: gout +5 (all 4 lanes), xo_b +1 (n), xo_g0/gp +4 (n), rout/bout 0; reset depths shifted with their data. PRICED: rp4a gout G 10 -> 15 per tile hop (parent BE_DELAY / GPAD re-solve)."
 },
